emu68 Driver Stack @PACKAGE_VERSION@
====================================
AmigaOS drivers for Raspberry Pi 4 / Compute Module 4 running Emu68.


BUILD VARIANT
-------------

  @DEBUG_BACKEND@
  @DEBUG_BACKEND_DESCRIPTION@

The 'off' archive is the normal download. The 'serial' archive is identical
except every driver also emits debug output, for troubleshooting.


COMPONENTS
----------

gic400.library @GIC400_VERSION@ (LIBS:)
  ARM GIC-400 interrupt controller library.
  Required by xhci.device, genet.device, nvme.device, and bcmpcie.library.
  The installer skips this automatically if a copy is already present in ROM
  or an expansion resident module.

bcmpcie.library @BCMPCIE_VERSION@ (LIBS:)
  BCM2711 PCIe bus library. Initialises the PCIe controller, enumerates
  devices, allocates BARs, and provides the driver API.

xhci.device (DEVS:USBHardware/)
  USB 2.0/3.0 host controller driver for the onboard OTG port and the VIA VL805
  chip present on every Raspberry Pi 4 board, in two mutually-exclusive lines -
  you pick ONE at install time. Poseidon itself is NOT part of this archive:
  choose the line matching the stack you already run.

    6.x @XHCI_VERSION@  for Poseidon for AmigaOS 6.x. Presents real USB 3.0
      devices to the stack (no USB 2.0 emulation) and supports USB 3.0 bulk
      streams, the fast UAS path for mass storage.

    5.x @XHCI_LEGACY_VERSION@  required on classic Poseidon 4.x, and also runs on
      Poseidon for AmigaOS 6.x, which keeps the older interface - but there it is
      the slower option: SuperSpeed devices are presented as USB 2.0 and there are
      no bulk streams. It rides in the archive under Storage/ and is installed to
      DEVS:USBHardware/ only if you choose it.

genet.device (DEVS:Networks/)
  Gigabit Ethernet for the Genet controller built into the Raspberry Pi 4 / CM4,
  in two mutually-exclusive lines - you pick ONE at install time:

    netdev  @GENET_VERSION@   the modern zero-copy driver for the bundled
      lwip-amiga TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library, below). NOT a SANA-II driver.

    SANA-II @GENET_SANA2_VERSION@  the classic driver for a third-party TCP/IP
      stack (Roadshow, AmiTCP, Miami). It rides in the archive under Storage/ and
      is installed to DEVS:Networks/ only if you choose it; its genet-stats
      counter tool then installs to C:.

bsdsocket.library @BSDSOCKET_VERSION@ (LIBS:)  [lwip-amiga @LWIP_VERSION@]
  A modern lwIP-based TCP/IP stack, installed with the netdev Ethernet line.
  Configures itself over DHCP the first time an application opens it; static
  addressing, hostname and driver selection live in ENVARC:netstack.prefs.
  Installing it REPLACES any existing bsdsocket.library (your current one is
  backed up to bsdsocket.library.orig first).

netdev-stats, netinfo, mdns (C:)
  Networking CLI tools installed with the netdev line. netdev-stats shows driver
  and interface counters; netinfo reports the interface and DNS configuration;
  mdns does multicast-DNS (.local) lookups and announcements.

nvme.device @NVME_VERSION@ (DEVS:)
  NVMe storage driver for PCIe-attached NVMe SSDs.

nvmeinfo, nvmeadm (C:)
  Diagnostic and admin CLI tools for nvme.device, installed automatically
  with the driver. nvmeinfo lists NVMe controllers and namespaces; nvmeadm
  reports SMART/health, identify, log pages, self-test, and firmware info.

openpci.library @OPENPCI_VERSION@ (LIBS:) [optional]
  Compatibility shim for software that calls OpenLibrary("openpci.library").
  Forwards calls to bcmpcie.library. Do NOT install if you have a real PCI
  expansion board (Mediator, Prometheus, G-REX, ...).

lspci (C:) [optional]
  CLI tool that lists all devices on the PCIe bus. Run from a Shell to
  verify the PCIe link is up and devices are enumerated correctly.


INSTALLATION
------------

Run the included 'Install' script using the Commodore Installer tool
(v43.3 or later, included with AmigaOS 3.1.4+).

Pick the drivers you want from the checklist, then choose ONE USB line (xhci 6.x,
xhci 5.x, or none) and ONE Ethernet line (netdev + lwip-amiga, SANA-II, or none)
when asked; the installer pulls in the libraries they need automatically, so you
cannot end up with a driver whose library is missing. It never downgrades a newer
copy already on your system - if an equal or newer version is installed, it asks
before replacing it. Three things are switched deliberately: the chosen
xhci.device line, the chosen genet.device variant and, on the netdev line,
bsdsocket.library are always (re)placed, since switching lines is a same-name
change that a version check would otherwise refuse.
gic400.library is skipped automatically when a copy is already resident in ROM
or an expansion module.

Manual installation: copy files to the destinations listed above and reboot.


REQUIREMENTS
------------

  - Emu68 (https://github.com/michalsc/Emu68) on Raspberry Pi 4 or CM4
  - AmigaOS 3.x
  - USB stack (for xhci.device): Poseidon, distributed separately. The 6.x
    driver line needs Poseidon for AmigaOS 6.x; the 5.x line runs on classic
    Poseidon 4.x and on 6.x alike
  - Networking (for genet.device): the netdev line uses the bundled
    bsdsocket.library (lwip-amiga); the SANA-II line needs a third-party TCP/IP
    stack such as Roadshow, AmiTCP or Miami


